Math","standard":"8.G.6","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"converse","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Geometry","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=55","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.G.6","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"converse","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Pythagorean reasoning and converse","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Squares on the legs of a right triangle have areas 625 and 3600. What is the area of the square on the hypotenuse?","answers":["4226","4224","4225","8450"],"correct":2,"explanation":"The hypotenuse square’s area equals the sum of the leg-square areas.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.G.6","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"area-identity","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Geometry","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=55","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.G.6","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","format":"area-identity","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Pythagorean reasoning and converse","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"A right triangle has legs 30 and 72. Find the hypotenuse.","answers":["79","78","77","156"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Apply a² + b² = c², using c for the longest side.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.G.7","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"hypotenuse","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Geometry","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=55","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.G.7","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"right-triangle","a":30,"b":72,"c":78,"unknown":"c"},"format":"hypotenuse","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Find unknown right-triangle sides","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"A right triangle has hypotenuse 5 and one leg 3. Find the other leg.","answers":["8","4","5","3"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Apply a² + b² = c², using c for the longest side.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.G.7","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"leg","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Geometry","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=55","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.G.7","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"right-triangle","a":3,"b":4,"c":5,"unknown":"b"},"format":"leg","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Find unknown right-triangle sides","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"In a right triangle, a student uses a leg as c in a² + b² = c². Why must the setup change?","answers":["c must be the side opposite the right angle, which is the longest side","c must always be a vertical side","The theorem works for every labeling without changes","c must always be the shortest side"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The squared hypotenuse equals the sum of the squared legs.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.G.7","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"hypotenuse-identification","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Geometry","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=55","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.G.7","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"right-triangle","a":24,"b":45,"c":51,"unknown":"c"},"format":"hypotenuse-identification","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Find unknown right-triangle sides","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"A ladder reaches 4 m up a wall, and its foot is 3 m from the wall. The wall and ground are perpendicular. How long is the ladder?","answers":["5","4","6","10"],"correct":0,"explanation":"The ladder is the hypotenuse of a right triangle.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.G.7","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"pythagorean-context","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Geometry","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=55","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.G.7","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"right-triangle","a":24,"b":45,"c":51,"unknown":"c"},"format":"pythagorean-context","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Find unknown right-triangle sides","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Find the distance between (-3, 1) and (0, 5).","answers":["6","4","5","10"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Use horizontal and vertical differences as the legs of a right triangle.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.G.8","mathGrade":8,"mathLevel":"practice","mathFormat":"diagonal-distance","difficulty":"intermediate","generatorVersion":4,"origin":"Original Ohio middle-school practice","subject":"Grade 8 · Geometry","source":"https://education.ohio.gov/getattachment/Topics/Learning-in-Ohio/Mathematics/Ohio-s-Learning-Standards-in-Mathematics/MATH-Standards-2017.pdf.aspx?lang=en-US#page=55","standardMeta":{"jurisdiction":"OH","code":"8.G.8","grade":8,"version":"2017","sourceId":"oh-math2017","scope":"Partial skill practice; not full-standard assessment","review":"Teacher review required","authoring":"Original program content","mathModel":{"kind":"coordinates","points":[[-3,1],[0,5]],"segments":[[0,1]]},"format":"diagonal-distance","coverageStatus":"Ready for teacher review","skillLabel":"Distance on the coordinate plane","contentSource":{"type":"prepared","label":"Saved generated practice"}}},{"text":"Point A is (-8, -7). Point B has x-coordinate -3 and is above A. Their distance is 13. Find B’s y-coordinate.","answers":["6","5","10","4"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Find the vertical difference with the Pythagorean theorem, then add it to A’s y-coordinate.","topic":"Math","standard":"8.G.8","mathGrade":8,"math